<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/05NB">Exercise <span data-tag="05NB">8.7.5.25</span>.</a> In the special case $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}= \Delta ^2$ and $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_0 = \Lambda ^{2}_{1}$, Proposition <a data-tag="05NA" href="/tag/05NA">8.7.5.24</a> reduces to the assertion that every inner fibration $U_0: \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}_0 \rightarrow \Lambda ^{2}_{1}$ fits into a pullback diagram </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix@R =50pt@C=50pt{ \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}_0 \ar [r]^-{F} \ar [d]^{U_0} &amp;  \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}\ar [d]^{U} \\ \Lambda ^{2}_{1} \ar [r] &amp;  \Delta ^2, } \]
</div>
<p> where $\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}$ is an $\infty $-category and $F$ is a categorical equivalence of simplicial sets (see Corollary <a data-tag="05N2" href="/tag/05N2">8.7.5.16</a>). Use the small object argument to give a more direct proof of this statement. </p>
</article>
